spec se04-self-conflict-through-frontier-lpg: 2 sessions, 2 permutations
# SE04. s0 holds its commit instant (the commit hold). s1 sets t.v = 1 through a lpg.Session and the
# commit acknowledges. s1 then rewrites its own node twice: SESSIONLESS (t.v = 2), whose
# snapshot is the held frontier, below s1's own commit, so it finds s1's version
# committed after its snapshot and is refused (first-updater-wins, F2); and through
# its SESSION (t.v = 3), which waits in the background for its own commit and, once
# s0 publishes, is not refused. The control interleaving publishes s0 first: both
# rewrites succeed.
# The sessionless rewrite is Graph.ApplyVersionedCtx; the session rewrite is Session.ApplyVersionedCtx.

starting permutation: s0w s0a s1w s1c s1sl s1aw s1wait s0p s1rel
step s0w: lpg: SetNodeProperty(s, v, 1)
step s0a: lpg: Graph.AllocateCommitTS (instant reserved, not published)
step s1w: lpg: SetNodeProperty(t, v, 1)
step s1c: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
step s1sl: lpg: SetNodeProperty(t, v, 2)
